+## Context
+
+`applyPatch` lives in `src/json-patch.ts` with an internal `deepEqual`. Patches must be minimal in spirit but need not be provably shortest.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Only `add`, `remove` and `replace` are emitted; no `move`/`copy` detection (keeps the diff simple and predictable).
+- Objects: remove members missing from `to`, recurse on shared members, add new members.
+- Arrays: strip common prefix and suffix, then compute an LCS (by `deepEqual`) of the middle. Walk it emitting `remove`/`add` at running indices; a removed+added pair at the same position is diffed recursively instead (yielding nested ops or `replace`).
+- Kind mismatch or differing scalars: `replace` at that path (root uses path `""`).
+- Values placed in the patch are cloned with `structuredClone`.
+- Operations are emitted in an order valid for sequential application (array indices tracked as the array evolves).
+
+## Risks
+
+- LCS is O(n·m) on the differing middle of an array; acceptable for typical payloads.
