+## Why
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document rather than the whole new version. The library can apply a JSON Patch but cannot produce one.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to`.
+- The patch is a diff: it recurses into objects and arrays so a small difference yields a small patch, never a whole-document replacement unless the root values are of different kinds.
+- Inputs are not mutated; the patch does not share mutable structure with them.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: adds a requirement for producing a patch from two documents.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/json-patch.ts` (new function, `deepEqual` exported for internal reuse), `src/index.ts`, tests, README.
+- No breaking changes, no new dependencies.
